# Client configuration — copy to `.env` to run the app:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# WHY THESE VALUES ARE IN A PUBLIC REPO, AND WHAT MUST NEVER JOIN THEM
#
# Every variable here is prefixed `VITE_`, which in Vite means "inline this into
# the client bundle at build time". All four are therefore ALREADY public: they
# ship inside the JavaScript that any visitor to the live site can download and
# read. Committing them exposes nothing that isn't exposed the moment the app
# loads in a browser. Verified 2026-08-23 before this file was created:
#
#   VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY  JWT claim `role` = "anon" — NOT service_role.
#                                  It is the public key every Supabase client
#                                  uses; RLS is what actually protects the data,
#                                  and auditing RLS is a standing job precisely
#                                  because this key is public by design.
#   VITE_APPLE_MAPKIT_TOKEN        A MapKit JS client token (ES256, team
#                                  P85MCK558V). Apple's design intent is that it
#                                  sits in a web page. Expires 2027-02-14 — see
#                                  the note at the bottom of this file.
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL / _PROJECT_ID  The project's public address.
#
# THE RULE: a value belongs in this file ONLY if it is safe on a billboard. A
# service_role key, a Stripe secret key (`sk_live_`/`sk_test_`), a webhook
# signing secret, or any Apple/Google private key MUST NEVER be added here, and
# must never carry a `VITE_` prefix at all — the prefix alone would publish it to
# every visitor. Server-side secrets live in Supabase edge-function secrets and
# in GitHub Actions secrets, and nowhere else.
#
# This file exists because `.env` is gitignored (.gitignore:59), so a fresh
# clone had no configuration and `createClient` threw at module scope before
# React ever mounted — the app served a permanently blank white screen with
# "supabaseUrl is required" in the console. That failure reads exactly like a
# code regression and has cost real debugging time more than once, most
# expensively in CI where the built iOS app hung on the boot loader.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://fncmgoasalhdgfwzhsqa.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImZuY21nb2FzYWxoZGdmd3poc3FhIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3Nzc2NDY1NDMsImV4cCI6MjA5MzIyMjU0M30.87hwQ90vpGPtaoIe0JOJvH6oxmabeWRSpomP5hIkhpY"
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="fncmgoasalhdgfwzhsqa"
VITE_APPLE_MAPKIT_TOKEN="eyJhbGciOiJFUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjRRQThKOVRBOEsiLCJ0eXAiOiJKV1QifQ.eyJpc3MiOiJQODVNQ0s1NThWIiwiaWF0IjoxNzg3MDI4MjA1LCJleHAiOjE4MDI1ODAyMDV9.IACOa7r9nrUZlH4lS7AzRMUhypCKozq-QUySuX63gooYc3C7syddU0bzzBTQSHiIFBMWrgc4XL0NO7lfTKL5qA"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_APPLE_MAPKIT_TOKEN is now a FALLBACK, not the primary source.
#
# The `mapkit-token` edge function mints short-lived (1 hour), origin-locked
# tokens from a private key that never leaves the server, and `useMapKitJs`
# asks it first — falling back to the static token above only when the server
# says "not configured" (503) or cannot be reached. So maps keep working today
# whether or not the secrets below are set.
#
# TO FINISH IT (removes the 2027-02-14 expiry entirely):
#   1. Apple Developer > Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles > Keys.
#      Use the EXISTING MapKit JS key 4QA8J9TA8K if you still have its .p8,
#      or create a new key with MapKit JS enabled and download the .p8 ONCE —
#      Apple will not let you download it again.
#   2. supabase secrets set \
#        APPLE_MAPKIT_PRIVATE_KEY="$(cat AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8)" \
#        APPLE_MAPKIT_KEY_ID=4QA8J9TA8K \
#        APPLE_MAPKIT_TEAM_ID=P85MCK558V
#   3. supabase functions deploy mapkit-token
#
# Once that is done the static token above can be deleted from this file and
# from the CI secrets — nothing will read it. Until then, leave it: it is what
# keeps maps alive if the function is unreachable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
